Deduplicate organization models in OrganizationDAO.searchWithoutFilters.

For a non-admin, searchWithoutFilters adds OrganizationSPARQLHelper
.addOrganizationAccessClause, which is a `{ group-hierarchy branch } UNION
{ no-group branch }`. When an organisation qualifies through the group
branch (a group is attached somewhere in its hasPart hierarchy and the
user is a member) the query can emit that organisation's URI on more than
one, non-contiguous row (different ?_userURI / ?publisher bindings). The
row->model mapper then produces two OrganizationModel instances with the
same URI.

Both the next statements reject that:
  - `new SPARQLListFetcher<>(... models)` + updateModels() throws
    "Multiple results with the same URI (...) at index N"
  - `userOrganizationCache.put(user.getUri(), models.stream()
     .collect(Collectors.toMap(OrganizationModel::getUri, identity())))`
    throws IllegalStateException on the duplicate key

so the whole GET /rest/core/organisations 400s / 500s for every non-admin
as soon as any organisation has a group. Admins are unaffected because
their branch skips the access clause.

Fix: collapse models to one per URI (first wins) before the list fetcher.
This matches what the cache toMap already assumes.

Present in 1.5.4 and unfixed on upstream develop as of 2026-09-02.
Reported upstream: TODO(link).

--- a/opensilex-core/src/main/java/org/opensilex/core/organisation/dal/OrganizationDAO.java
+++ b/opensilex-core/src/main/java/org/opensilex/core/organisation/dal/OrganizationDAO.java
@@ -183,6 +183,18 @@
             });
         }

+        // The non-admin access clause (addOrganizationAccessClause) can return the
+        // same organisation on more than one non-contiguous row (reachable both
+        // through a group in its hierarchy and through the "no group" branch),
+        // which survives as duplicate models. Both SPARQLListFetcher below and the
+        // userOrganizationCache.put(... toMap ...) reject duplicate URIs, so
+        // deduplicate here, keeping the first occurrence.
+        Map<URI, OrganizationModel> distinctModels = new LinkedHashMap<>();
+        for (OrganizationModel model : models) {
+            distinctModels.putIfAbsent(model.getUri(), model);
+        }
+        models = new ArrayList<>(distinctModels.values());
